Subject: bgpd: reinitialize EVPN state when reviving a hidden VPN instance

The retained default instance skips fresh allocation. Its EVPN cleanup has
already freed the containers; initialize those again and restore ownership.
The nexthop table survives hidden teardown and must be released before init.
Owner restoration follows upstream ab390ba48bb9f8c5d7650fe066a58945d0a61d14.

--- a/bgpd/bgpd.c
+++ b/bgpd/bgpd.c
@@ -3968,6 +3968,21 @@
 		bgp_ls_init(bgp);
 	}
 
+	/* A hidden default instance survives deletion for its VPN RIB, but
+	 * teardown released its EVPN containers. Recreate them before the
+	 * revived instance can be inspected or used for EVPN again.
+	 */
+	if (hidden && !bgp->vnihash) {
+		bgp_evpn_nh_finish(bgp);
+		bgp_evpn_init(bgp);
+	}
+
+	/* Restore the EVPN owner skipped by the hidden peer_init path.
+	 * Mirrors upstream ab390ba48bb9f8c5d7650fe066a58945d0a61d14.
+	 */
+	if (hidden && inst_type == BGP_INSTANCE_TYPE_DEFAULT && !bgp_get_evpn())
+		bgp_set_evpn(bgp);
+
 	/*initialize global GR FSM */
 	bgp_global_gr_init(bgp);
 
